  "limitations": [
    "13 of16 selected images: all8 normals and final pixels S/SW/W/NE/E. NW/N/SE final pixels remain on quality HOLD for internal-alpha holes introduced during background extraction. Normal-stage PASS is not pair PASS.",
    "The historical root images and catalog depict a different3-cell design and remain unchanged. Do not mix those images with this new ceramic candidate as a coherent single-character set.",
    "Four foot roots and occlusion remain a design hypothesis. S retains broad frontal foot faces; corrected SW shows broad faces with thin side edges; W-v2 shows thin side depth. Exact rigid roots are unproven.",
    "The accepted S image has wider and more separated feet than the initial numerical proposal. Actual selected-image continuity is the reference; the initial dimensions are not claimed to be achieved.",
    "Exact body thickness, camera yaw,45-degree spacing and common in-game scale are unverified.",
    "Pixel versions simplify shade levels, grain and contours; highlights and foot edges can be stronger.",
    "Application binding/catalog migration, game changes, runtime acceptance and production adoption are outside this Draft.",
    "Historical incomplete candidates and the prior safety hold remain separately preserved; this new design does not resolve the old request outcome.",
    "The selected SW, E and NE pixels use approved two-stage paths: selected normal alone to opaque pixel intermediate, then intermediate-only background extraction. It is not a direct normal-to-final single call; extraction can alter small contour/color details.",
    "N foot spacing is slightly wider and visible breadth slightly narrower than S; E side width is about7 percent smaller than W at the same image extent. These are representative artistic views, not exact metric geometry.",
    "W/E sidewalls have no unique markings; handedness relies on the adjacent views and creation record, not on a distinct mark in either side view.",
    "Opaque intermediate pixel renders are not included. NW failed transparent versions are quality-HOLD; unfinished pixel processing is not silently counted as selected."
